	(footprint "Connector_FPC:AFC01-S40FCA-00"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "194dbf97-bcf7-422b-98dd-c0d21f8f4feb")
		(at 147 110)
		(descr "Jushuo AFC01-S40FCA-00 (LCSC C262674), 40-position 0.5mm-pitch bottom-contact ZIF FPC connector, SMT right-angle. Hand-authored. Pad geometry (0.50mm pitch, 0.30x1.30mm signal pads, 19.50mm pin1-pin40 span at -9.75..+9.75mm, 2.00x1.60mm mounting pads 1.70mm beyond pin1/pin40 in X, 2.68mm signal-row-to-mounting-pad offset in Y) is sourced from the authoritative EasyEDA/JLCPCB official library footprint for this exact LCSC part (C262674, FPC-SMD_AFC01-S40FCA-00, fetched via easyeda.com's public component API, 2026-11-15) -- not the LCSC-hosted datasheet PDF (https://www.lcsc.com/datasheet/C262674.pdf), which turned out on direct text-extraction to be a generic company reliability/process spec book with no dimensioned CAD drawing at all, so there is no LCSC-spec-table dimension to confirm it against. Round-4 fix: the round-3 fix moved the 40 signal pads to the corrected Y position but left the body outline (F.Fab), courtyard (F.CrtYd), silkscreen lines, pin-1 marker and REF** text at their old coordinates, so all of them collided with the moved pads (courtyard too small to enclose pads 1-40; silkscreen and fab lines running through the pad row; pin-1 dot sitting on top of pad 1). Re-derived this round from the same EasyEDA footprint's non-pad shapes (ComponentShape/3DModel/TopSilk layers, same API fetch, 2026-11-15), converting EasyEDA's internal units to mm with the 0.254mm/unit scale factor (cross-checked against the known 0.5mm pin pitch): F.Fab body outline x=+-12.20mm, y=-2.33..3.02mm (asymmetric -- the housing overhangs further on the actuator/flip-lock side than the contact-tail side, so it does legitimately extend over the pad footprints from a top-down view, same as the real connector housing). F.CrtYd x=+-12.70mm, y=-3.60..3.30mm (encloses the body outline and all 42 pads with >=0.25mm margin on every side). F.SilkS top/bottom lines moved to y=3.16 / y=-3.60, both clear of every pad's Y range (no pad extends above y=0.80 or below y=-3.33). Pin-1 marker moved to (-10.44,-2.82) -- next to pad 1's left edge (pad 1 spans x=-9.90..-9.60), not on top of it. REF** text moved to y=-4.30, clear of the courtyard. Still a simplified axis-aligned approximation of the connector's true stepped housing shape, not a literal trace of it -- needs a human KiCad-GUI DRC pass before PCB fab.")
